<title>SWITZERLAND: SIG shoots for two-digit 97 profit growth.</title>
<headline>SIG shoots for two-digit 97 profit growth.</headline>
<dateline>NEUHAUSEN, Switzerland 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>SIG Schweizerische Indistriegesellschaft (SIG) chief executive David Syz said he hoped the mechanical engineering group could post double-digit gains in sales and operating profit in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Such growth is possible for sales at current exchange rates,&quot; he told Reuters, adding this applied to operating profit as welll.</p>
<p>SIG lifted 1996 group net to 88.6 million Swiss francs from 70.1 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
